  "notes": [
    "Chaos run: The first worker's listener closes and its connections are reset; it listens again when the fault ends. The agent reports FAILED within one heartbeat and the registry drops the worker within a refresh, so this is a registry-plus-retry baseline, not a breaker test.",
    "What this embedded mock cluster cannot show here: Whether the circuit breaker detects a crash: the registry gets there first. It shows that a crash costs the clients nothing the retry cannot absorb, and that nothing regresses. A real process kill (SIGKILL) differs in that the OS resets connections the same way, but also frees the port for a replacement.",
    "Windows follow when the fault was really applied and cleared. Gateway counters (attempts per request, retries) are read at the tick that opens and closes a window (every 1s), so an attempt of a request in flight at a boundary falls in the next window; the per-request figures come from the clients.",
    "Closed-loop clients: 14 for the whole run on 32 request slots (24 left serving). Closed-loop clients wait for each response, so a failing worker also slows the offered load.",
    "Load average (1, 5 and 15 minutes) at the start of the run: 3.51 3.97 4.28; at the end: 2.69 3.67 4.15."
  ],
